records.eligibility:
- Medically certified by a qualified doctor to have visual impairment; 
- aged 5 years and above; 
- assessed by a social worker, orientation & mobility instructor, and/or occupational therapist to benefit from one or more services provided.

- Resident of South West District
- Applicant or care recipient must be Singaporean;
- Per capita household income ≤ $1,500 or blue CHAS card holder;
- Caregiver and care recipient must reside in the same household; and
- Care recipient requires assistance with min. 3 activities of daily living (ADLs): washing / feeding / dressing / toileting / mobility; OR
- Care recipient has a certified permanent disability: physical / visual / hearing / intellectual / autism / others.
